  <!-- ============================================================
       HYDRODYNAMICS — drag in water

       NOTE: this plugin previously read

           <linear_drag>40 40 80</linear_drag>
           <angular_drag>5 5 5</angular_drag>

       Neither element exists in gz-sim-hydrodynamics-system. They were parsed
       as unknown tags and silently dropped, so the vehicle had NO drag at all
       and simply accelerated under its net buoyancy — a free ascent from the
       spawn point put it 21 m up in under 9 s. The real parameter names are
       the per-axis damping coefficients below (negative = opposes motion):

         xU / yV / zW      linear damping, N per m/s
         kP / mQ / nR      angular damping, N.m per rad/s
         *absU / *abs*     the quadratic pair for each, left at 0 here

       Values carry over the intent of the old tags. Linear damping is the
       original 40/40/80. Angular damping is scaled up from the original 5/5/5
       because the thrusters moved outboard on the bigger frame, lengthening
       every moment arm; these hold peak rotation rates at what 5/5/5 would
       have given on the old 0.50 m frame:

         roll   17.4 N.m / 11 = 1.58 rad/s   (old geometry:  7.8 / 5 = 1.56)
         pitch  18.0 N.m /  9 = 2.00 rad/s   (old geometry: 10.2 / 5 = 2.04)
         yaw    30.1 N.m /  9 = 3.35 rad/s   (old geometry: 17.0 / 5 = 3.39)

       Real damping is dominated by the quadratic terms, and added mass is not
       modelled at all — both belong to the Phase 5 tuning pass. This is the
       linear-only model the SDF always meant to have, now actually applied.
       ============================================================ -->
  <plugin
    filename="gz-sim-hydrodynamics-system"
    name="gz::sim::systems::Hydrodynamics">
    <link_name>base_link</link_name>

    <xU>-40</xU>      <xUabsU>0</xUabsU>
    <yV>-40</yV>      <yVabsV>0</yVabsV>
    <zW>-80</zW>      <zWabsW>0</zWabsW>

    <kP>-11</kP>      <kPabsP>0</kPabsP>
    <mQ>-9</mQ>       <mQabsQ>0</mQabsQ>
    <nR>-9</nR>       <nRabsR>0</nRabsR>
  </plugin>

</model>
</sdf>
